{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17163 - PROTEIN:6138",
  "verbalization": "Norarecoline is implicated in the regulation of the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Norarecoline acts as a target of multiple compounds, which in turn target the proteasome subunit. Specifically, Norarecoline is linked to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is a target of two different compounds—2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and Phorone. Both of these compounds are known to interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the proteasome. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the proteasome subunit supports the hypothesis that Norarecoline may influence proteasome function through these interactions. The evidence is consistent with a role in proteasome regulation, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
